      "explanation": "Completing the square gives $y=-(x+2)^2+5$. The parabola opens downward, and its axis of symmetry is $x=-2$. For a downward-opening parabola, $y$ increases as $x$ increases to the left of the axis of symmetry, so $x<-2$.",
